Med</source><year>2007</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>665</fpage><lpage>674</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18073579</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><collab>CDC National Office of Public Health Genomics</collab><source>Evaluation of Genomic Applications in Practice and Prevention: Gene Expression Profiling for Breast Cancer Management and Prognosis</source><year>2008</year><publisher-name>Atlanta: CDC National Office of Public Health Genomics</publisher-name></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Ginsburg</surname><given-names>GS</given-names></name><article-title>Genomic medicine: 'Grand challenges' in the translation of genomics to human health.</article-title><source>Eur J Hum Genet</source><year>2008</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>873</fpage><lpage>874</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/ejhg.2008.115</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18560443</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B14"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Hudson</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Javitt</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Burke</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Byers</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><article-title>ASHG Statement on direct-to-consumer genetic testing in the United States.</article-title><source>Obstet Gynecol</source><year>2007</year><volume>110</volume><fpage>1392</fpage><lpage>1395</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18055737</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B15"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Uhlmann</surname><given-names>WR</given-names></name><name><surname>Guttmacher</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name><article-title>Key internet genetics resources for the clinician.</article-title><source>JAMA</source><year>2008</year><volume>299</volume><fpage>1356</fpage><lpage>1358</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="